{"chars": "And right in the middle is the orchid's most special secret: the column. In most flowers, the part that makes pollen and the part that catches pollen grow separately. In an orchid, they are fused together into one little column. And in most orchids, the pollen isn't loose and dusty, the way it is in other flowers. It is packed into tiny sticky bundles called pollinia (pol-IN-ee-uh), which stick onto a visiting insect and ride away with it to the next flower.", "start": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 0.637, 0.637, 0.637, 0.713, 0.713, 0.713, 0.713, 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 1.137, 1.137, 1.137, 1.262, 1.262, 1.262, 1.262, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.413, 1.875, 1.875, 1.875, 1.875, 1.875, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.15, 2.562, 2.562, 2.562, 2.562, 2.562, 2.562, 2.562, 3.3, 3.4, 3.4, 3.4, 3.4, 3.5, 3.5, 3.5, 3.5, 3.5, 3.5, 3.5, 4.225, 4.338, 4.338, 4.338, 4.475, 4.475, 4.475, 4.475, 4.475, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 4.725, 5.275, 5.35, 5.35, 5.35, 5.35, 5.45, 5.45, 5.45, 5.45, 5.45, 5.737, 5.737, 5.737, 5.737, 5.737, 5.85, 5.85, 5.85, 5.85, 5.85, 5.85, 6.125, 6.125, 6.125, 6.125, 6.125, 6.125, 6.125, 6.487, 6.487, 6.487, 6.487, 6.588, 6.588, 6.588, 6.588, 6.675, 6.675, 6.675, 6.675, 6.675, 6.975, 6.975, 6.975, 6.975, 6.975, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.1, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.875, 7.875, 7.875, 7.875, 7.875, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 8.188, 9.1, 9.225, 9.225, 9.225, 9.338, 9.338, 9.338, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.425, 9.9, 9.975, 9.975, 9.975, 9.975, 9.975, 10.125, 10.125, 10.125, 10.125, 10.238, 10.238, 10.238, 10.238, 10.238, 10.238, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.575, 10.938, 10.938, 10.938, 10.938, 10.938, 11.175, 11.175, 11.175, 11.175, 11.363, 11.363, 11.363, 11.363, 11.363, 11.363, 11.363, 11.65, 11.65, 11.65, 11.65, 11.65, 